One thing before the code: in a no-signal basement, "send each field as soon as it's filled in" will fail by definition. The approach is still fine if the tablet **saves each field to local storage first** (IndexedDB/SQLite) and treats the send as a background sync from a durable outbox that retries until the server acknowledges it. The client should only mark a field as synced after it gets a 2xx.

That shapes the endpoint. Since requests will be retried, delayed, duplicated, and arrive out of order, it needs to be idempotent, and it should never discard data. So I made it append-only, with a "current value" table derived from it.

